    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Merge queue — what lands next, and as what",
      "prov:value": "Bean `hfag`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean hfag"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Handing a PR to the queue — the sibling session's side (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Both are ROLES, not sessions. Owner, 2026-10-04: *\"Merge Manager may\nchange\"*. So nothing in this section depends on which session holds either\nlane.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "The PR is the message",
      "prov:value": "A\ncomment posted anywhere else reaches nobody: not on a PR you believe is the\nsteward's, and not on an issue such as #1800. Measured 2026-10-03/04 (bean\n`j5iq`): a merge-order change was posted to #1959 three hours after it\nmerged, and the pokes on #1800 changed none of the three facts that kept\n#1968 out of the queue.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean j5iq",
        "#1800",
        "#1959",
        "#1968",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "After submitting: do not spend CI you do not need yet",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-04: once CI has confirmed the PR, a submitter far back in the\nqueue should not burn CI cycles keeping up with a churning `main`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The steward's side: reach a submitter who has fallen behind",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-10-04: a steward handed back a dozen PRs in one session with\n  comments and queue entries only. The owner asked *\"why did you have a\n  process failure here?\"*. The procedure lived in another skill\n  (`merge-conflict-patterns`) that the steward never loaded, and nothing\n  checked for it. Owner: \"Backfill + enforce\". The 13 beans were backfilled\n  (`mfhc` and twelve more).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Address the ROLE, never a session",
      "prov:value": "Owner,\n2026-10-04: use one when it is the more efficient tool, and say how you used\nit.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The steward answers in the queue, and the queue lives on the beans branch",
      "prov:value": "**Where to read it depends on the state-branch cutover** (arc `fs43`, bean\n`9ofm`). Bean `ugxd` moves the queue to its OWN branch,\n`cat/cat-harness/merge-queue`, ahead of `fs43` — §\"Where the queue is GOING\"\nbelow — and where the two disagree, that section is the newer plan:\n- **Before the cutover**, `main` is authoritative.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9ofm",
        "bean ugxd",
        "bean main",
        "arc fs43"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The steward answers in the queue, and the queue lives on the beans branch",
      "prov:value": "It is not offered on a personal-account\nrepository (bean `1hjm`). The merge guard (`bun run cat merge:guard <pr>`,\nbean `uoob`) checks the six submission points mechanically; run it against\nyour own PR before you announce.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 1hjm",
        "bean uoob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The steward answers in the queue, and the queue lives on the beans branch",
      "prov:value": "## Where the queue is GOING, and the tool that will write it (bean `najo`)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean najo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the queue is GOING, and the tool that will write it (bean `najo`)",
      "prov:value": "For the two days after the graph was declared it therefore held **no\nentry at all**: the one actor whose decisions it records was the one actor that\ncould not write to it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the queue is GOING, and the tool that will write it (bean `najo`)",
      "prov:value": "`merge:queue:read` exits 4 and\n  `readQueueEntries` THROWS when the branch is not mounted, because \"no\n  decisions recorded, all clear\" printed over a graph nobody read is `dh4f`. `merge:steward` feeds recorded overrides into\n  the table's `ownerOverride` input and their positions into the order, treats\n  an un-cleared ejection as refused, and prints a live hold. Until 2026-10-04 it\n  passed none of them: a decision nobody reads back is a decision nobody took.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Admission asks which runs are OWED, never whether anything is red",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-10-02 on #1889's head `7ab6119405`:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1889",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Admission asks which runs are OWED, never whether anything is red",
      "prov:value": "So a filter for `conclusion == \"failure\"` returns nothing, and three suites\ncompleted having executed nothing at all. **Counting the runs does not catch\nit either** — nine were present and every expected name matched. Only asking\n*which runs are owed for this event* catches it, and\n`check-head-has-run` is the one\nthing here that asks (bean `3pqn`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3pqn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Admission asks which runs are OWED, never whether anything is red",
      "prov:value": "`unknown` is handed back, never admitted and **never reported as red** (bean\n`0qjq`): telling somebody their head is unverified when you merely could not\nlook trains them to ignore the signal, which costs more than the gap.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0qjq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Admission asks which runs are OWED, never whether anything is red",
      "prov:value": "`workflow_dispatch` is the designed\nworkaround for the bot-actor push condition (bean `0qjq`, and `merge-main.yml`\ndispatches the gating workflows for exactly that reason), but a dispatched run\nis evidence about the TREE, not evidence that the owed `pull_request` run\nexists. The session that wrote this section made that error on #1888 — read\neight dispatched jobs as \"green\" because the names matched — and\n`check:head-has-run` caught it. Report the two facts separately or the\ndistinction is lost.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0qjq",
        "#1888"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Overlap has a KIND, and a train is the right answer to one of the four",
      "prov:value": "That is not hypothetical. `merge:overlap` over all 36 open PRs on 2026-10-02\n(459 pairs) found **#1907 × #1909 `independent: false` with\n`authored_overlap = 0`** — colliding on `package.json` and generated regions\nonly. **A pipeline that treats that like a content collision builds trains\nnobody needed.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1907",
        "#1909",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A train admits only members that STACK cleanly (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling, 2026-10-04 ~17:40Z:** *\"require that a merge train has PRs\nthat are stacked one on top of another. You're wasting too much time resolving\nconflicts in the train and blocking other stuff from happening.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A train admits only members that STACK cleanly (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**Why, measured on train `merge-train-2026-10-04a` (#2113):** two members with\n`declared` conflicts took **about an hour and five pushes** to reach green:\n1. The train tool dropped the gitignored-but-tracked LSI files (bean `u4up`).\n2. That drop staled the auto-docs pages.\n3. Another session landed #2112, and the train conflicted again.\n4. Re-merging `main` took a 12-minute regen.\n5. A semantic conflict surfaced: #2043 imported a module that #2112 had moved.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean u4up",
        "#2113",
        "#2112",
        "#2043",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Regenerate on a clean tree, and check it",
      "prov:value": "The precondition does not make the count stable, and saying so is the point: two\nmembers each adding a file still write different integers to one line. Bean\n`y7b3` measured 76 of 300 replayed merges conflicting on `beans/README.md`,\nevery one on the `| defs/ | N files |` line — and the class is wider than that\nbean states: **54 generated READMEs across 14 instances carry 207 such rows**\n(measured 2026-10-02). `merge:main` already resolves them under\n`readme-generated-regions`, so the residual cost falls on merges made by plain\ngit rather than by the pipeline.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean y7b3",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A PR lands only through `merge:guard` (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "The script\n(`cat-harness-tools/scripts/merge-guard.ts`, bean `uoob`, child (f) of `nok9`) is\nthe merge: it evaluates eight checks over GitHub's live facts, and performs\nthe PUT, pinned to the head it evaluated, only when every one passes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean uoob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A PR lands only through `merge:guard` (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "### When no Merge Manager is active, the owning session merges (owner ruling 2026-10-06)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When no Merge Manager is active, the owning session merges (owner ruling 2026-10-06)",
      "prov:value": "No workflow posts a `merge-guard` commit status any\nmore (owner, 2026-10-23: \"i dont want the merge guard check\";\nfolio-assistant#2662 removed `.github/workflows/merge-guard.yml`), so there\nis no posted verdict to read in its place.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "folio-assistant#2662",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "When no Merge Manager is active, the owning session merges (owner ruling 2026-10-06)",
      "prov:value": "Owner ruling 2026-10-03, after three PRs were landed unfinished by a steward\ncalling the PUT directly on the same day:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "When no Merge Manager is active, the owning session merges (owner ruling 2026-10-06)",
      "prov:value": "A `workflow_dispatch` run\n   counts **only** as the stand-in for a `pull_request` run GitHub held for\n   approval (`action_required`, bean `0qjq`) on a head that is a merge-main\n   bot merge: merge-main has already merged main into that head, so the head\n   IS the merge, and a dispatch on it judges the tree that would land. A green dispatch never rescues a `pull_request` run that\n   executed and went red (#1937), and anywhere else it is reported and **not**\n   counted. **Feature Staging is judged, never waited for** (owner ruling\n   2026-10-05, bean `gnnj`): a staging run still in flight, or not started,\n   is not a refusal — its deploy is held by the #1956 `gh-pages` rate limit,\n   measured at up to 41 min with eight previews queued — and the verdict\n   says so as **not waited for**. Once it finishes, red still refuses, since\n   `stage` runs real checks before it deploys — **unless the only failed\n   step is the deploy itself** (`DEPLOY_ONLY_STEP`): a push window that\n   never opened, or three rejected pushes, is not a verdict on the tree\n   (owner ruling 2026-10-05). **`mergeable`** — GitHub says the head still merges cleanly into `main`\n   (bean `vihx`). Check 5's runs tested the head merged with `main` **as\n   `main` was when the head was pushed**; once `main` moves, a stale green\n   head with a valid marker passed checks 1-7 while it conflicted (#1898,\n   and two HTTP 405 \"merge conflicts\" refusals on 2026-10-05).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0qjq",
        "bean gnnj",
        "bean vihx",
        "#1937",
        "#1956",
        "#1898",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the authors stall: the steward dispatches unblockers",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-04, verbatim: *\"dispatch agent to handle where CI isnt green.\nmake sure you dont use up all github workspace\"* and *\"if there is something\nsmall an agent can handle that unblocks, then do so\"*. Authors' sessions hit\nusage limits together, so the whole hand-back column can go quiet for an hour\nwhile every member in it is one small fix away from admission.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Stalled for days, with no handover report: write it, then hand it to a takeover agent",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-04, verbatim: *\"several agents (~8) just stalled for week.\nthey didnt generate handover reports. disaptach agent to review PRs and\ngenerate plan ... to takeover work by anotther agent\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Landing",
      "prov:value": "A member admitted against the old `main` can turn `dirty` and\nthen cannot land at all. Measured 2026-10-04: #2059 was admitted at\n`f8e1006d`, then reported `dirty` once #2069 landed. Its tested head is still\ngreen, but GitHub refuses to merge a conflicted PR, so it waits for its\n`merge:main` round and fresh CI on the new head.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2059",
        "#2069",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Landing",
      "prov:value": "Only with the owner's release, which is now the authorisation half of\n[`merge-to-main`](merge-to-main.md) (`Call_MergeToMain` in `merge-train.bpmn`;\nit was `Task_Release` until 2026-10-09): explicit, or a standing ruling\nquoted verbatim with its date, and **only through `bun run cat merge:guard <pr>\n--merge --session <id>`** (section above).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Landing",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-04, verbatim: *\"my approcal - that counts for the PRs\nthat are in queue. new PRs need my approval exp-licity (through you or\nsiblign)\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Landing",
      "prov:value": "## Post-merge asymmetry: why main needs its own regeneration pipeline (bean ey1c)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Post-merge asymmetry: why main needs its own regeneration pipeline (bean ey1c)",
      "prov:value": "### The accidental-repair pattern (observed 3 times in 2 hours)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The automated post-merge repair pipeline",
      "prov:value": "**NEGATIVE CONTROL:** A merge that changes nothing counted triggers 0 repairs\n   and opens NO PR (`status: \"clean\"`, exit 0), preventing churn (bean `do70`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean do70"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-33",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "ACK every PR that enters the queue, on its bean (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-04: *\"as part of merge manager skill you need to ACK a new PR\nin queue on its bean\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-34",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every open PR has an entry: review the whole list, then triage it",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-04, verbatim: *\"review all open PRs.... anything not in merge\nqueue? put in as status unknown any found. then try to figure out where they\nare, what's stale, etc.\"* and *\"add to merge manager skills.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-35",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every open PR has an entry: review the whole list, then triage it",
      "prov:value": "Measured on the first\nreview: #2082 was approved as a three-bean close, and an hour later its\nbranch carried an 11-file code change under a new title. The typed fix is a `release`\nbound to `releasedSha` (the zmdo session's draft on #2065); until it lands,\nthis check is the steward's.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2082",
        "#2065"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-36",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Your merge cadence is an input to the bot's throughput",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-10-03 over the last 100 runs of that workflow (bean `o8s9`):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean o8s9",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-37",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A hold has an EXPIRY and a trigger, or it outlives its reason",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, 2026-10-03. A steward froze merges so a `merge-main` sweep could\nfinish without being cancelled — correct at the time, and the owner confirmed\nthe order. The sweep finished. The hold did not. It then survived three more\nsweeps, and the steward kept reporting \"held for ordering\" while four PRs sat\nclean and green for roughly forty minutes. The owner had to ask *\"what is\nblocker on merging?\"* to end it. The answer was the steward.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-38",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Sweep the whole queue; a tracked handful is not the queue",
      "prov:value": "The same session that held four green PRs\nwas also unaware of two others that had opened and gone green in the\nmeantime — they were not in its mental list, so they were in no list at all."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-39",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Sweep the whole queue; a tracked handful is not the queue",
      "prov:value": "**`no failures and nothing pending` is NOT green, and this rule got that wrong\non its first use. The sweep that followed it marked #1953 mergeable on\n`ok=1 bad=0 wait=0` — one completed check, the `.jsonld siblings` one, against\nthe 23 that a full suite produces here. Nothing had failed and nothing was\npending because **almost nothing had been asked**. That is bean `1xhc` inside\nthe sweep itself: a gate that did not fire is indistinguishable from one that\npassed, and a tally of failures cannot tell them apart.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 1xhc",
        "#1953"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-40",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read `base.ref` BEFORE anything else: a stacked PR is not a main-queue member",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, 2026-10-03. PR #1937 was based on `claude/quirky-davinci-ixuymr`,\nanother PR's branch. Every check the steward ran was against `origin/main`:\n`rc=0`, 16/16 green, all true and all irrelevant. The merge went to the stacked\nbase, the PR closed as merged, and its nine commits were not on `main`. It took\na second PR to re-land, and a sibling agent independently misdiagnosed the\nabsence as a force-push eating a merge — a scarier cause than the truth, with a\ndestructive remedy attached.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1937",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-41",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Read `base.ref` BEFORE anything else: a stacked PR is not a main-queue member",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, 2026-10-23.** cat-harness#439 was\nstacked on #432's branch, and its body said exactly that. #432 merged, then\n#439 merged eight seconds later: into #432's branch, not `main`. The same head\ncommit had to be re-landed as #478.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "cat-harness#439",
        "#432",
        "#439",
        "#478",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-42",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`git add -A` after a merge silently reverts the submodule gitlinks",
      "prov:value": "This is bean `ygga` one layer\ndeeper, and it defeats the check that bean prescribes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ygga"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-43",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`git add -A` after a merge silently reverts the submodule gitlinks",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, 2026-10-03, on #1819. Main had moved `bootstrap` to `ebfa406` and\n`bootstrap-tools` to `3046412`; the branch never touched either, so the\nthree-way merge correctly took main's side, and `git add -A` undid it. The\nsymptom was not a submodule error — it was `regen` reporting **five checks as\n\"a real defect, not staleness\"** (`readme:sync` in its four spellings plus\n`translate-bpmn:bootstrap`), all of them one module-load failure:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1819",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-44",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A local gate run in a contended container is not evidence — and here is the ratio",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-10-03. A full `bun test` shard in this container: **14,625\ntests across 715 files in 1438.88 s**. The workflow's own comment puts the same\nshard at **2 m 07 s – 2 m 21 s** on a dedicated runner. That is roughly **ten\ntimes slower**, at load average **11** with three concurrent `bun test` runs and\na `regen` belonging to other sessions.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-45",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A local gate run in a contended container is not evidence — and here is the ratio",
      "prov:value": "**Two ways this measurement was nearly got wrong, both bean `0s6w`:**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0s6w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-46",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Agentic pre-merge review: warn-only and the would-have-blocked counterfactual",
      "prov:value": "Bean `h1uq`. Owner ruled agentic merge review **warn-only** on 2026-10-02 and confirmed 2026-10-03: *\"warn only. proposal predates ruling, update it.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean h1uq",
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-47",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tool-integrated agentic pre-merge review (CodeAgent / 2402.02172v5)",
      "prov:value": "Evaluated under bean `gs0u` and codified in [`methodologies/agentic-pre-merge-review.md`](../../../methodologies/agentic-pre-merge-review.md).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean gs0u"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-48",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tool-integrated agentic pre-merge review (CodeAgent / 2402.02172v5)",
      "prov:value": "Judged Boundary (Owner ruling 2026-10-02/10-03, bean `nok9`)**:\n   Deterministic compile gates (Lean formal proofs, SUSHI/FHIR IG AST, JSON-LD schema renders,\n   linter and test suites) answer questions with one computable truth — **these MUST BLOCK**. **The 49% False-Positive Guard**: Standalone LLMs exhibit up to 48.58% false-positive\n   rates in code vulnerability detection (arXiv:2402.02172v5, Table 2). An automated review gate\n   must never block merge on unverified LLM assertions, which induce severe alert fatigue. Promotion from warn to block requires measured calibration against recorded repository\n   defects (`plj1`, `dh4f`, `w4tq`, `7u3g`).\n3.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean nok9",
        "bean dh4f",
        "bean w4tq",
        "bean 7u3g",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-49",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the authors stall: the steward dispatches unblockers",
      "prov:value": "| rule | why |\n|---|---|\n| **at most ONE push per PR**, after `bun run cat gates` locally — or, when every conflict was generated, after the targeted checks of [`merge-conflict-patterns`](merge-conflict-patterns.md) §\"A merge round — run each check ONCE\" | each push runs full CI **and** deploys a staging preview into `gh-pages`, which has a size budget. Pushing speculatively spends both |\n| no `workflow_dispatch`, re-run, empty commit or close/reopen | the same budget, and a dispatched run is not an owed run (above) |\n| merge commits only: no rebase, amend or force-push | it is somebody else's branch |\n| authored conflict → resolve only dead code, or a pure addition carried over verbatim; otherwise quote both sides and stand down | choosing between two behaviours is the author's call |\n| `git submodule update --init` and `bun run cat state:mount` before `regen` | without the submodules `merge:steward` cannot load. Without the mount, `fsh-guts:viz:check` exits non-zero (it judges that the mounted graph renders; the page itself is built at publish, bean `0b8c`) and `audit:coverage:strict` goes red |\n| delete the worktree's `node_modules` at the end | four parallel installs run out of the container's disk |\n| one comment per PR: root cause, the commit it pushed or the reason it stood down | the author comes back to an explanation, not a mystery commit |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0b8c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-50",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the authors stall: the steward dispatches unblockers",
      "prov:value": "**After any merge of `main`, check for silently dropped files.** Some files\nunder `*/test/results/` (LSI indexes, QA and detangle sidecars) are gitignored\nbut still tracked. Once a resolution step removes one from the index, regen\nrewrites it on disk and `git add -A` does not stage it again. Local checks\nstill pass, but CI's fresh checkout fails. `merge:main` and the merge-main bot\nnow refuse such a merge and name the paths (`droppedInMerge` in\n`merge-base.ts`, see `merge-conflict-patterns` §\"When one side deleted the\nfile\"). A hand `git merge` gets no such check. After one, run\n`git diff --diff-filter=D HEAD^1 HEAD -- '*/test/results/*'`, and restore\nanything that main still tracks with `git checkout HEAD^2 -- <path>` (bean\n`8j9e`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8j9e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-51",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Regenerate on a clean tree, and check it",
      "prov:value": "The fix is bean `ba9e`: take the integer off `main` into the KG's `_data`\nlayer, which classifies `take-base` and is therefore already auto-resolved by\n`merge-conflict-patterns.ts:171`. Not `-merge` and not a merge driver — both\nare refused in `.gitattributes` on measured grounds, the first because it\ntidies conflicts without removing them and the second because it needs\nper-checkout `git config`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ba9e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-52",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the queue is GOING, and the tool that will write it (bean `najo`)",
      "prov:value": "**The pairing with `workflows/` is what this cost.** The queue held the\ndecisions and a finished train run next door held the evidence they met, in one\nstore. `beans/` is still on `main` until arc `fs43` lands (beans `9ofm`,\n`p3ny`), so for now the two are one `state:mount` apart. That trade was made\nknowingly: the pairing was costing the graph every one of its nodes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p3ny"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-53",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where derived artefacts are regenerated",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-06, options \"1 3\": each PR regenerates its own derived files before merge, and the release build regenerates before it publishes; no bot pushes to main and no repair PRs.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-54",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where derived artefacts are regenerated",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-06: \"preview builds not required regen\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-55",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where derived artefacts are regenerated",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-06: \"full runs only on manual trigger OR release build\". The PR regen became a dispatch naming the PR, and the hourly post-merge tick was removed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-queue.md#provenance-56",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A PR lands only through `merge:guard` (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "CI gates a release only (owner, card Q-CIB-4 A, 2026-11-08, after *\"CI not gate on non-release merge to main\"*): on a non-release merge `merge:guard` check 5 is advisory.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-08",
        "Q-CIB-4"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-08"
      ]
    }
  ]
